{"id":"0aac2b51-e1f0-4bd3-96ab-a6b0d34c389e","object":"chat.completion","created":1784884816,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    word_token_indices = case['word_token_indices']\\n    word_labels = case['word_labels']\\n    token_count = case['token_count']\\n    \\n    # Validate number of word groups matches number of labels\\n    if len(word_token_indices) != len(word_labels):\\n        raise ValueError('Mismatch between word groups and labels count')\\n    \\n    token_labels = [0] * token_count\\n    assigned = [False] * token_count\\n    \\n    for indices, label in zip(word_token_indices, word_labels):\\n        for idx in indices:\\n            if idx < 0 or idx >= token_count:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Token index {idx} out of range [0, {token_count-1}]')\\n            if assigned[idx]:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Token index {idx} appears in more than one word group')\\n            assigned[idx] = True\\n            token_labels[idx] = label\\n    \\n    # Check all tokens are covered\\n    for i in range(token_count):\\n        if not assigned[i]:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Token index {i} is not covered by any word group')\\n    \\n    # Build kept_indices from token_labels == 1\\n    kept_indices = [i for i, lbl in enumerate(token_labels) if lbl == 1]\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'kept_indices': kept_indices,\\n        'token_labels': token_labels\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write Python code for solve(case) that satisfies the given objective. The case payload contains: word_token_indices (list of lists of ints), word_labels (list of ints), token_count (int). We need to produce kept_indices (list of ints) and token_labels (list of ints of length token_count). Each word group (list of token indices) gets its word label broadcast to each token index. Then we keep those token indices whose label is 1. The token_labels vector should have length token_count, each entry is the label for that token (0 or 1). The kept_indices are the indices where token_labels==1, in order.\n\nConstraints: Validate: each word group's tokens must be within [0, token_count-1], no overlapping tokens across word groups, all tokens from 0 to token_count-1 must be covered exactly once (no gaps, no overlaps). Also word_labels length must equal number of word groups. If any violation, raise ValueError.\n\nReturn dict with kept_indices and token_labels.\n\nWe must output JSON with \"implementation\" key containing the source code as a JSON string.\n\nLet's craft the code accordingly."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1258,"completion_tokens":593,"total_tokens":1851,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":896},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":246},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":896,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":362},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}